# SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog - Cursor Rules

## Article Creation Workflow

### 1. File Structure & Creation Process
- Articles: `src/app/articles/[slug]/page.tsx` (kebab-case slugs)
- Add to: `src/data/articles.ts` (at beginning for newest date)
- SEO Components: Use `src/components/seo/` components for metadata

### 2. Article Interface
```typescript
interface Article {
  title: string;           // Required
  description: string;     // Required: 2-3 sentences
  slug: string;           // Required: kebab-case
  date: string;          // Required: "Month DD, YYYY"
  imageUrl?: string;     // Optional: Unsplash URLs
  googleDoc?: string;    // Optional: Source research
  deepResearch?: boolean; // Optional: Comprehensive analysis
  youtubeUrl?: string;   // Optional: Video content
  isVideo?: boolean;     // Optional: Video flag
  options?: boolean;     // Optional: Options trading
  pinned?: boolean;      // Optional: Pin to top
  bookSummary?: boolean; // Optional: Book summary flag
  noSummary?: boolean;   // Optional: Skip summary
  podcastUrl?: string;   // Optional: Spotify podcast URL
}
```

### 3. Required Components
- **Return to Home button** in header:
```tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { ArrowLeft } from 'lucide-react';

<div className="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
  <Link href="/" className="inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-blue-800 hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors duration-200 text-white font-medium">
    <ArrowLeft className="mr-2 h-4 w-4" />
    Return to Home
  </Link>
</div>
```

- **SEO Components** (MANDATORY for all articles):
```tsx
import { articles } from '@/data/articles';
import { StructuredData, BreadcrumbStructuredData } from '@/components/seo/structured-data';

// In component
const currentArticle = articles.find(article => article.slug === 'your-article-slug');

// In return statement
<>
  {currentArticle && (
    <>
      <StructuredData article={currentArticle} />
      <BreadcrumbStructuredData articleTitle={currentArticle.title} articleSlug={currentArticle.slug} />
    </>
  )}
  {/* Your content */}
</>
```

- **Navigation sidebar** with smooth scrolling and IntersectionObserver
- **Interactive components** with `'use client';` and React hooks

### 4. Badge Positioning
- **"Deep Research"**: Top-left corner (purple)
- **"Video"**: Top-right corner (red)
- **"Podcast"**: Top-right corner (green) - when no video
- **"Options"**: Bottom-right corner (orange-yellow)

### 5. Content Styling
- Use research callouts, strategy boxes, risk warnings
- JSX arrows: `&rarr;` not `→`
- Responsive design with Tailwind CSS
- Educational disclaimers
- **Footer branding**: `© 2025 SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog. Educational content for informational purposes only.`

### 6. Flags Usage
- `deepResearch: true` for comprehensive analysis
- `options: true` for options trading content  
- `isVideo: true` for video content
- `bookSummary: true` for book summaries
- `pinned: true` for featured articles
- `podcastUrl: "spotify-url"` for podcast episodes

### 7. Content Categories
- **Deep Research**: Comprehensive analysis with multiple sections, interactive elements
- **Options Trading**: Put/call strategies, Greeks, volatility analysis
- **Video Content**: YouTube integration with embedded players
- **Podcast Content**: Spotify podcast integration with dedicated buttons
- **Stock Analysis**: Company-specific DCF models, valuation analysis
- **Book Summaries**: Interactive summaries of trading/investment books

### 8. Technical Requirements
- Use `'use client';` for interactive React components
- Implement smooth scrolling navigation
- Add proper TypeScript typing
- Include responsive design for mobile/desktop
- Use semantic HTML structure with proper heading hierarchy
- **MANDATORY: Include SEO components on every article**

### 9. SEO Implementation (CRITICAL)

#### 9.1 Branding Standards
- **Site Name**: "SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog"
- **Domain**: https://sophie-ai-finance.com
- **Author**: "SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog"
- **Publisher**: "SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog"
- **Twitter Handle**: @sophies_daddy

#### 9.2 Article SEO Pattern
```tsx
'use client';

import { articles } from '@/data/articles';
import { StructuredData, BreadcrumbStructuredData } from '@/components/seo/structured-data';

export default function YourArticle() {
  const currentArticle = articles.find(article => article.slug === 'your-slug');
  
  return (
    <>
      {/* SEO Components - MANDATORY */}
      {currentArticle && (
        <>
          <StructuredData article={currentArticle} />
          <BreadcrumbStructuredData articleTitle={currentArticle.title} articleSlug={currentArticle.slug} />
        </>
      )}
      
      {/* Your article content */}
    </>
  );
}
```

#### 9.3 Metadata Requirements
- **Title Format**: `Article Title | SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog`
- **Description**: Use article.description from articles.ts
- **Keywords**: Include relevant SEO keywords based on content type
- **Open Graph**: Automatic via SEO components
- **Twitter Cards**: Automatic via SEO components
- **Structured Data**: JSON-LD schema for articles

#### 9.4 Image Requirements
- **Article Images**: Prefer 1200x630 for social sharing
- **Alt Text**: Descriptive and SEO-optimized
- **Fallback**: Default to `/images/agents/SOPHIE.png`

### 10. Quality Standards
- Articles should be educational, not investment advice
- Include proper disclaimers and risk warnings
- Cite sources when using external research
- Use professional language and formatting
- Test all interactive features before publishing
- **MANDATORY: Include SEO components on every new article**

### 11. Common Patterns
- Navigation sidebars with active highlighting
- Strategy comparison boxes and tables
- Risk callouts with warning styling
- Research citations with external links
- Interactive elements (calculators, charts) when appropriate

### 12. SEO Automation
- **Sitemap**: Auto-generated via `next-sitemap` on build
- **Robots.txt**: Auto-generated with proper directives
- **Structured Data**: Automatic via SEO components
- **Social Meta**: Automatic via layout and article components

### 13. Podcast Integration

#### 13.1 Podcast URL Configuration
- Add `podcastUrl: "https://open.spotify.com/episode/EPISODE_ID"` to article data
- Use full Spotify episode URLs (not embed URLs)
- Example: `podcastUrl: "https://open.spotify.com/episode/49kYVr5A7CQT31Un6Faeqp"`

#### 13.2 Article Card Integration
Podcasts automatically appear in ArticleCard with:
- **Green "Podcast" badge**: Top-right corner of image (when no video)
- **Metadata link**: Small "Podcast" link in article metadata
- **Action button**: Prominent green "Podcast" button with music icon

#### 13.3 Article Page Integration
```tsx
// Import Music icon
import { Music } from 'lucide-react';

// In call-to-action section
{currentArticle?.podcastUrl && (
  <a 
    href={currentArticle.podcastUrl}
    target="_blank" 
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    className="inline-block bg-green-600 text-white font-bold py-4 px-8 rounded-lg text-lg hover:bg-green-700 transition-colors duration-300 transform hover:scale-105"
  >
    <Music className="inline mr-2" />
    Listen to Podcast
  </a>
)}
```

#### 13.4 Podcast Button Styling
- **Primary**: Green background (`bg-green-600`) with white text
- **Hover**: Darker green (`hover:bg-green-700`) with scale effect
- **Icon**: Music icon from Lucide React
- **Theme**: Consistent with Spotify branding

#### 13.5 Badge Priority
- Video badge takes priority over podcast badge
- Only show podcast badge when `podcastUrl` exists and `isVideo` is false
- Position: `absolute top-2 right-2` with green gradient

## General Development Guidelines
- Always follow existing code patterns and conventions
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Maintain responsive design principles
- Follow the established component structure
- Test thoroughly before implementing changes
- **CRITICAL: Every article MUST include SEO components**

## SEO File Structure
```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── seo/
│   │   ├── structured-data.tsx     # JSON-LD schema components
│   │   └── article-seo.tsx         # SEO helper functions
│   ├── stock/
│   │   ├── stock-fundamentals-analysis.tsx  # Financial Health + video
│   │   └── stock-valuation.tsx     # DCF/EV-EBITDA + videos
│   └── ui/
│       └── video-tutorial.tsx      # Reusable video component
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx                  # Main SEO metadata
│   ├── stock/
│   │   └── [ticker]/
│   │       └── page.tsx            # Stock analysis pages
│   └── articles/
│       └── [article-name]/
│           └── page.tsx            # Include SEO components
└── data/
    └── articles.ts                 # Article metadata

public/
├── sitemap.xml                     # Auto-generated
├── robots.txt                      # Auto-generated
└── manifest.json                   # PWA manifest

Root:
├── next-sitemap.config.js          # Sitemap configuration
└── .cursorrules                    # This file
```

## Build Process
1. **Development**: `npm run dev`
2. **Build**: `npm run build` (auto-generates sitemap)
3. **Deploy**: Sitemap and robots.txt included automatically

## Video Tutorial Integration for Stock Analysis

### 1. VideoTutorial Component
- **Location**: `src/components/ui/video-tutorial.tsx`
- **Purpose**: Reusable component for embedding educational YouTube videos
- **Usage**: Stock analysis sections (Financial Health, DCF, EV/EBITDA, etc.)

### 2. VideoTutorial Component Interface
```tsx
interface VideoTutorialProps {
  title: string;           // Tutorial title (e.g., "DCF Tutorial: Step-by-Step Guide")
  description: string;     // Educational description
  videoId: string;        // YouTube video ID (not full URL)
  startTime?: number;     // Optional start time in seconds
  className?: string;     // Optional additional CSS classes
}
```

### 3. Implementation Pattern
```tsx
import { VideoTutorial } from "@/components/ui/video-tutorial";

// Example usage in stock analysis components
{analysisMethod === "dcf" && (
  <VideoTutorial
    title="DCF Tutorial: Step-by-Step Guide"
    description="Learn how to build a DCF model from scratch and understand the key assumptions."
    videoId="DEzMJY7dJ6o"
    startTime={6}
    className="mb-4"
  />
)}
```

### 4. Video Tutorial Guidelines
- **Hidden by Default**: Videos should not auto-play or be visible on page load
- **Toggle Functionality**: Include "Show Video" / "Hide Video" button
- **Contextual Placement**: Place tutorials within relevant analysis sections
- **Educational Focus**: Videos should explain methodology, not provide investment advice
- **Performance**: Videos only load when user chooses to view them

### 5. Current Video Tutorials
- **Financial Health**: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qOzB4WtPRok
- **DCF Analysis (Absolute Valuation)**: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DEzMJY7dJ6o&t=6s
- **EV/EBITDA Analysis (Relative Valuation)**: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_cJfQ_qKmM&t=15s
- **AI Agent Analysis**: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QkRPgEI5PZM

### 6. Adding New Video Tutorials
- Use the reusable VideoTutorial component
- Extract video ID from YouTube URL (e.g., `DEzMJY7dJ6o` from `youtube.com/watch?v=DEzMJY7dJ6o`)
- Add `startTime` prop if video should start at specific timestamp
- Place within the relevant analysis method's conditional rendering
- Follow consistent naming pattern: `[Method] Tutorial: [Description]`

### 7. Design Standards
- **Blue theme**: `bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/30` with blue borders
- **Compact spacing**: `p-3`, `mb-2`, `mb-3` for reduced visual footprint
- **Button styling**: Blue background with hover effects and transitions
- **Responsive video**: `aspect-video` ratio with `max-w-2xl` constraint

## Quality Checklist for New Articles
- [ ] Added to `src/data/articles.ts` at the beginning
- [ ] Includes SEO components (`StructuredData` + `BreadcrumbStructuredData`)
- [ ] Has proper Return to Home button
- [ ] Uses correct badge positioning
- [ ] Includes educational disclaimer
- [ ] Footer has "SOPHIE Daddy Quant Blog" branding
- [ ] Tests build process to ensure sitemap generation
- [ ] Responsive design verified
- [ ] Interactive elements tested
- [ ] Podcast integration (if applicable): badge, metadata link, and action button working 